comments.body:
> I’m fine with skipping for the next few years (assuming amd64 does not lose its dominance); ideally we would have the image multi-arch and easily re-buildable (not the case currently), but I don’t know whether we have any convention set up for that nowadays. Podman maintainers?

@timcoding1988 is supposed to audit our test images and generate instructions on how to create them. Once we have that we can rebuild things multi arch where needed.

But overall multi arch wise we lost a huge part of CI infra with the cirrus shutdown. While the CNCF provided infra do offer arm runners they are VMs and cannot do nested virt unlike x86_64 and as such the lima setup is just not viable. Once could try to work around that by using a privileged container as OS where the tests run but it would not be able to run the proper full test suite then AFAIK. So in that sense testing on arm got a lot more complicated.
